WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.135
-The movie "Wonder Woman"
had a huge opening

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:04.738
at the box office this weekend.

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:07.707
It became the first female-led
superhero blockbuster ever.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.241
But people
have differing opinions

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:10.776
about the praise
the film has received.

00:00:10.776 --> 00:00:13.646
To make sure you get to see
the issues from both sides,

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.783
we've invited two of our writers
with contrasting points of view.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:17.951
We'll examine their opinions

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:20.386
in a segment we call
"Point, Counterpoint."

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.288
♪♪

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.524
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:30.229
Ally and Amber, thank you for
being here to discuss this film.

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:32.165 line:0%
First question --

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:35.435 line:0%
"Wonder Woman" grossed over
$100 million this weekend.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:38.871 line:0%
Is this a definitive triumph
for women in film, Ally?

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:40.339 line:0%
-It absolutely is.

00:00:40.339 --> 00:00:42.375
But let's not pat ourselves
on the backs

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:45.077
just because Hollywood made
one blockbuster movie

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.546
with a female protagonist.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:50.416
Women only account for 32% of
all speaking roles in movies.

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:51.651
A real triumph would be

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:54.119
to be bringing that ratio
to half and half.

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:55.622
-Half and half. Amber?

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:58.057
-Half and half is delicious.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:59.625
Have you ever had it?

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:03.897
It's like if milk and ice cream
had a very yummy baby.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.132
You can put half and half
in your coffee

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.434
or you can just
put sprinkles in it

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:11.304
and drink it straight
and have a party in your mouth.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.172
-Wait. What?

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.874 line:0%
-Moving on.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.243 line:0%
"Wonder Woman" is the first
successful superhero movie

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.644 line:0%
directed by a woman.

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:20.379 line:0%
Do you think
this will encourage studios

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:22.548 line:0%
to put more women
behind the camera? Ally?

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:23.849
-I certainly hope so.

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:26.585
Right now only 7% of Hollywood
directors are women.

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:29.055
But I will say the true
glass ceiling will be broken

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.324
when studios give
female directors big budgets,

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.659
even after they have
a box-office flop,

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:35.462
just like they do
with male directors.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.764
There's still a lot of work
to be done to achieve equality

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.298
in our nation's film canon.

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:41.034
-Strong words. Amber?

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.569
-I think cannons are great.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:46.271
Especially when they're filled
with confetti!

00:01:46.271 --> 00:01:49.508
One time, I jumped out
from behind my grandma's couch

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:51.310
and shot off a confetti cannon,

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:55.148
and the whole room filled with
tiny sparkles and she fainted.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.482
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.482 --> 00:02:00.520
And when she came to,
she whispered, "That was fun."

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.755
-[ Laughs ] Your grandma
sounds like a great lady.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.657
-She is. Hey, Nana!

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.159
-Seth, she's talking
about confetti

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.127
when the topic
is "Wonder Woman."

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:11.764
-These are things I wonder
as a woman!

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.565
You know what else I wonder?

00:02:13.565 --> 00:02:16.135
Could I do
a Daryl Hall impression?

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.738
♪ You're a rich girl,
and you're going too far ♪

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.940
♪ But you know
it don't matter anyway ♪

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.475
I can!
-You can.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:25.945
I thought he was right here.
That was amazing.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.780 line:0%
Next up.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.383 line:0%
Also breaking records this year,
the movie "Get Out",

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.585 line:0%
which had a black lead
and a black director.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.855 line:0%
Could this lead to more films
for underserved audiences? Ally?

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:39.792
-Seth, every time a demographic
that isn't white male and 18-34

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.228
comes out to support something,
corporate America is shocked.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.431
Why? We have jobs, we make
money, and we spend that money.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.800
The fact that minorities
are a powerful economic force

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.268
shouldn't be a surprise.

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:50.970
-Well said. Amber?

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.672
-You know what's a surprise?
This.

00:02:53.672 --> 00:02:55.141
[ Bang ]
-Aah! Oh, my God!

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.709
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.978
Amber!

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.080
[ Applause ]

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.049
-Now...

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:05.285
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:13.459
[ Both laughing ]

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.161
-Just real quick.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:17.062
Let's step out of the scene
for a minute and talk --

00:03:17.062 --> 00:03:19.632
talk about how long
we rehearsed this today.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:23.202
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.772
I shot it backwards onto myself!

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.874
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.943
-You two were backstage saying,

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:33.413
"Oh, it's so easy.
It's just a button."

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:36.682
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:41.587
-I just accidentally shot it
right every other time.

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:44.056
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:45.491
Oh!

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:48.327
-All right.

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:51.263
-The point is, Amber shooting
herself with a confetti cannon

00:03:51.263 --> 00:03:52.698
is off topic.

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:54.600
It has nothing to do with
what we are talking about.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.903
-Ally, this isn't
"Point, Point."

00:03:57.903 --> 00:04:02.107
It's "Point, Counterpoint."
Okay, Ally?!

00:04:02.107 --> 00:04:06.045
You get a point,
and then Amber gets a point!

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.213
That's how it works, Ally!

00:04:08.213 --> 00:04:10.549
-Fine. Did we get it all?

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:13.018
-Yes. You look beautiful.

00:04:13.018 --> 00:04:14.386
-Thanks, Amber.

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:16.922 line:0%
-And finally.

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:19.492 line:0%
"Wonder" -- [ Laughs ]

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:22.094 line:0%
"Wonder Woman" has been
a big hit with critics.

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:24.630 line:0%
But why do you think
it's resonating with audiences?

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:28.100
-You know what, Seth?
I have an answer for that,

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.269
but I won't waste my time
because I'm sure Amber

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.705
has something ridiculous
to say or do, don't you?

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.607
-Actually, I don't.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.376
I saw "Wonder Woman"
this weekend,

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:39.278
and when I saw it, I cried.

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:42.247
It resonated with me
because I was so moved

00:04:42.247 --> 00:04:46.519
by seeing a strong powerful
woman represented on screen.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.223
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:52.825
It's impossible
to put into words...

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:56.128
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:59.098
...what that movie
meant to women

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:04.069
or how much that movie can
change the lives of young girls.

00:05:04.069 --> 00:05:05.905
-Wow. Amber, that --

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:07.806
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:11.009
That was beautiful.

00:05:11.009 --> 00:05:12.912
Beautifully delivered.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:15.147
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:19.051
-That was --
That was truly beautiful.

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:21.520
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.888
That was so much more beautiful

00:05:22.888 --> 00:05:24.524
than anything Ally
has said or done.

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.358
-Okay. Okay.

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:29.328
-I also think what's
equally important is...

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:30.797
[ Bang ]

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.331
-Yay!

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:34.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.903
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.409
-Amber, stop doing that.
That's rude.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.811
-You're right.
Where are my manners?

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:47.913
-Oh! Thank you.

00:05:47.913 --> 00:05:49.615
[ Bang ]
-All right.

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:51.551
-Yay!
-That was fun.

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:54.186
-This has been
"Point, Counterpoint."

00:05:54.186 --> 00:05:56.255
We'll be right back
with Courtney Love.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:58.591
[ Laughter ]

